#!/usr/bin/env python3
from pathlib import Path
import re,json
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2];out=root/'docs/reports/cliff-a-refinement'
log=(out/'refined.log').read_text();m=re.search(r'PROTOTYPE triangles=(\d+) masses=\d+ quads=(\d+) ngons=(\d+) chips=(\d+)',log)
tri,quads,ngons,chips=map(int,m.groups())
(out/'status.json').write_text(json.dumps({'status':'selected_A_refinement_enabled','triangles_in_isolated_wall':tri,'quad_faces':quads,'larger_polygon_faces':ngons,'localized_chips':chips,'remaining':['Original terrace bands and some constrained narrow faces remain','Visual review against target still needed; no exact-match claim','No controlled frame-time benchmark or WASM check']},indent=2)+'\n')
items=[('a-before.png','Selected A'),('refined.png','Refined A'),('a-before-wire.png','A — triangle topology'),('polygons.png','Refined A — polygon boundaries')]
cells=''.join(f'<figure><figcaption>{label}</figcaption><div class="crop"><img src="{name}"></div></figure>' for name,label in items)
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Selected A — polygon facets and broken transitions</title><style>*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#20272b;color:#e9dfd0;font:17px/1.55 system-ui}main{max-width:1500px;margin:auto;padding:28px}a{color:#9cdbcd}p{max-width:1120px}h2{margin-top:36px}.wide{overflow:auto}.sheet{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);width:max-content}.sheet figure{border:2px solid #536167;margin:0}.sheet figcaption{height:40px;background:#2d383d;padding:5px 16px;font:600 20px/30px system-ui}.crop{width:1220px;height:400px;position:relative;overflow:hidden}.crop img{position:absolute;width:2880px;height:1800px;left:-820px;top:-160px;max-width:none}img.full{max-width:100%;height:auto}.status{padding:15px;border-left:5px solid #94c9b1;background:#2b383c}code,pre{color:#e8c48c}</style><main><h1>Selected A: broader polygon facets and broken junctions</h1><p class="status">A is now the basis of the generated cliff-face pass. The isolated refinement and native game capture are below. Changes remain uncommitted. This is progress toward the supplied reference, not an exact-match claim.</p><p><a href="comparison.png">Comparison image</a> · <a href="game.png">Current native game, 160% zoom</a> · <a href="triangles.png">Actual GPU triangle wireframe</a> · <a href="specification.png">Supplied annotated specification</a></p><h2>Same selected wall and camera</h2><p>The first row compares selected A and refined A. The second compares A's triangle topology with the refined logical polygon boundaries. Internal GPU diagonals are omitted only in that polygon-boundary view; the linked triangle-wireframe capture shows the actual triangulation. All native captures use the same 160% game camera, lighting, materials, seed and player position. These identical pixel crops are enlarged 2× for viewing.</p><div class="wide"><div id="refinement-sheet" class="sheet">'''+cells+'''</div></div><h2>What changed</h2><p>Retained A's irregular two-dimensional network and coherent surface relief. Suitable adjacent triangles are joined into convex quad planes. Shared interior vertices are relaxed toward those planes, with the upper/lower contours fixed. Pairs that remain noticeably nonplanar stay triangles, and merged planes with aspect ratios above 2.5 are rejected. A sparse set of sharp interior junctions is truncated into small polygon chips and short shelf-like surfaces. Chip locations and widths vary; transitions are not bevelled uniformly.</p><p>The isolated wall now has <strong>'''+str(quads)+''' quad faces, '''+str(ngons)+''' larger polygon faces and '''+str(chips)+''' localized chips</strong>, rendered as '''+str(tri)+''' triangles. Logical polygons are triangulated for the GPU; every triangle receives its actual geometric normal. No random colors or fabricated shading normals were added.</p><p>The runtime collector now retains short connecting contour edges and processes longer connected wall sections, including the slanted-but-steep foot faces used by the isolated A experiment. The original source contour alternates right-angle grid edges; treating each turn as a geological break was reproducing the vertical columns. The selected A chart now spans those connecting steps instead. Small ledges below 1.15 m, tiny patches and invalid remeshes retain their original faces to keep the mesh budget bounded.</p><h2>Enabled game view</h2><a href="game.png"><img class="full" src="game.png"></a><p>This is the regular native executable with the selected pass enabled, not the diagnostic substitution. Other eligible cliff faces now use the same method. The camera, materials, lighting and decoration placement systems are unchanged. Cast shadows respond naturally to changed geometry.</p><h2>Validation</h2><p><a href="facet-checks.log">30 focused patch checks</a>: fixed floor/top contours; deterministic vertices and connectivity; mixed faces/chips; manifold UV coverage; bounded mesh sizes and predominantly steep surfaces. <a href="canyon-checks.log">Twelve seeded map checks</a>: unchanged floor/cap vertices, terrain elevations and decoration positions; collision invariance; reachability/clearance checks and the existing mesh budget. <a href="render-checks.log">Native rendering/asset checks</a>: five seeds in both themes, 22,147 placements and actual rendered mesh rays. <a href="build.log">Native build</a>. No WASM check under the standing waiver.</p><p>The vertical render-ray test now compares the globally nearest rendered hit, as the existing oblique-ray test already did. Broad facets can cross renderer chunk boundaries. Each probe still has to hit its own source chunk, and the 3 mm distance tolerance is unchanged.</p><p>The first integration exceeded the existing mesh budget. Leaving small ledges on the original surface resolved that without raising the budget. A filesystem-full interruption was resolved by removing rebuildable ASAN object/archive files; source files and assets were retained.</p><h2>Reversible controls</h2><p>In <code>assets/visual/canyon.cfg</code>, <code>polygon_facets 0</code> restores the preceding face-detail pass. <code>irregular_facets 0</code> disables face detail entirely. Restart after changing the file. Footprints, cliff heights, terrace layouts, collision, room connectivity and combat are unchanged.</p><h2>Remaining limitations</h2><p>The original terrace bands, cliff-top silhouettes and some narrow faces are intentionally retained. The changes improve face structure but do not recreate the target's whole rock-mass composition. Small contour-forced slivers remain. Further art-direction review is needed; no exact visual match is claimed. No controlled frame-time benchmark or exhaustive seed sweep was run.</p><h2>Reproduce the isolated comparison</h2><pre>DW_CLIFF_FREEZE_SURROUNDINGS=1 DW_CLIFF_OPTION=a2 \\
 ./build/deathward_cliff_alternatives --mute --smoke --theme canyon \\
 --style original --scene profile-works --frames 60 --screenshot refined.png
# DW_CLIFF_WIRE=1: polygon boundaries; DW_CLIFF_WIRE=triangles: GPU edges.</pre><p>The debug freeze keeps the preceding face pass outside the selected wall, so its A comparison remains controlled. The enabled native game view intentionally applies the refinement to other eligible cliffs too.</p></main></html>'''
(out/'index.html').write_text(html)
